hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1171,"[1171] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, that he had heard that Urwah ibn al-Zubayr used to say about the son of the cursed one, and he was born Adultery: If he dies, his mother inherits his rights according to the Book of God Almighty, and his brothers give his mother their rights, and he inherits The survivor is the slave of his mother, if she is your slave, and if she is an Arab, she inherits her rights, and his brothers inherit from his mother. Their rights, and what remained for the Muslims was a foothold in front of Malik Hadith: 1171 Arabic Hadith:"
1176,"[1176] Yahya told me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Talha ibn Abdullah ibn Awf - he said, and he was the most knowledgeable of them. Thus - on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman bin Awf: that Abdul-Rahman bin Awf divorced his wife while he was ill. So Othman bin Affan inherited it from him, after her waiting period had expired. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1176 Arabic Hadith:"
1191,"[1191] Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’: that Abdullah bin Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, according to a covenant. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Omar ibn al-Khattab asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He ordered it, so let him review it. Then He may keep her until she is pure, then she will menstruate, then become pure, then if he wishes he may keep her after that, and if he wishes he may divorce her before he touches her, so he may The waiting period for which God has commanded women to be divorced - Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 1191 Arabic Hadith:"
1203,"[1203] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’: that Abdullah ibn Umar divorced his wife in the residence of Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was on his way to the mosque, so he used to take the other route from the backs of the houses, as he did not want to He asks her permission until he comes back to her. \\nMutta Imam Malik Hadith: 1203 Arabic Hadith:"
1209,"Malik said, ""Neither a free man nor a slave who divorces a slave- girl nor a slave who divorces a free woman, in an irrevocable divorce, is obliged to pay maintenance even if she is pregnant, and he cannot return to her."" Malik said, ""A free man is not obliged to pay for the suckling of his son when he is a slave of other people, nor is a slave obliged to spend his money for what his master owns except with the permission of his master"
1210,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab said
1211,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating in the time of the Messenger of Allah
1212,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Urwa ibn az- Zubayr from A'isha
1213,Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said that he heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman say
1214,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi and Zayd ibn Aslam from Sulayman ibn Yasar that al-Ahwas died in Syria when his wife had begun her third menstrual period after he had divorced her. Muawiya ibn Abi Sufyan wrote and asked Zayd ibn Thabit about that. Zayd wrote to him
1215,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abu Bakr ibn Abd ar-Rahman and Sulayman ibn Yasar and Ibn Shihab used to say
1216,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said
1217,"Yahya related to me from Malik from al-Fudayl ibn Abi Abdullah, the mawla of al-Mahri that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Salim ibn Abdullah said, ""When a woman is divorced and begins her third period, she is clearly separated from him and is free to marry again"
1218,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Ibn Shihab and Sulayman ibn Yasar all said
1219,"Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say, ""The idda of the divorced woman is reckoned by the menstrual cycles even if she is estranged ."" (The reason the idda is normally reckoned by the menstrual cycle is to see whether the woman is pregnant or not)"
1220,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from a man of the Ansar that his wife asked him for a divorce
1221,Yahya related to me from Malik thal Yahya ibn Said heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Sulayman ibn Yasar both mention that Yahya ibn Said ibn al-As divorced the daughter of Abd ar-Rahman ibn al-Hakam irrevocably
1222,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that the daughter of Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl was the wife of Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Uthman ibn Affan
1223,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar divorced one of his wives in the house of Hafsa
1224,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab was asked who was obliged to pay the rent for a woman whose husband divorced her while she was in a leased house. Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1225,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Yazid
1226,"Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard Ibn Shihab say, ""The woman who is absolutely divorced does not leave her house until she is free to remarry. She has no maintenance unless she is pregnant. In that circumstance the husband spends on her until she gives birth."" Malik said, ""This is what is done among us"
1227,"Malik said, ""What is done among us when a slave divorces a slave- girl when she is a slave and then she is set free, is that her idda is the idda of a slave-girl, and her being set free does not change her idda whether or not he can still return to her. Her idda is not altered."" Malik added, ""The hadd-punishment which a slave incurs is the same as this. When he is freed after he has incurred but before the punishment has been executed, his hadd is the hadd of the slave."" Malik said, ""When a free man divorces a slave-girl three times, her idda is two periods. When a slave divorces a free woman twice, her idda is three periods."" Malik said about a man who had a slave-girl as a wife, and he bought her and set her free, ''Her idda is the idda of a slave-girl, i.e. two periods, as long as he has not had intercourse with her. If he has had intercourse with her after buying her and before he set her free, she only has to wait until one period has passed . "" Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said and from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt al-Laythi that Said ibn al-Musayyab said, ''Umar ibn al-Khattab said, 'If a woman is divorced and has one or two periods and then stops menstruating, she must wait nine months. If it is clear that she is pregnant, that is that. If not, she must do an idda of three months after the nine, and then she is free to marry"
1228,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1229,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab said
1230,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Ali ibn Abi Talib said about the two arbiters about whom Allah
1231,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umar ibn al-Khattab
1232,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Abdullah ibn Masud said that there was nothing binding on someone who said
1233,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab that Said ibn al- Musayyab said
1234,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab about whether the deadline was set from the day he had married her
1235,Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said
1236,Yahya related to me from Malik that Ibn Shihab said that he had heard Said ibn al-Musayyab
1237,Yahya related to me from Malik from Thabit ibn al-Ahnaf that he married an umm walad of Abd ar-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab. He said
1238,Yahya related to me from Malik that Abdullah ibn Dinar said
1239,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa that his father said
1240,Yahya related to me from Malik from Thawr ibn Zayd ad-Dili that Allah
1241,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar were asked about a man who divorced when he was drunk. They said
1242,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab said
1243,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdu Rabbih ibn Said ibn Qays that Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman said that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abu Hurayra were asked when a pregnant woman whose husband had died could remarry. Ibn Abbas said
1244,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar was asked about a woman whose husband died while she was pregnant
1245,Yahya related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn 'Urwa from his father that al-Miswar ibn Makhrama told him that Subaya al-Aslamiya gave birth a few nights after the death of her husband. The Messenger of Allah
1246,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Sulayman ibn Yasar that Abdullah ibn Abbas and Abu Salama ibn Abd ar-Rahman ibn Awf differed on the question of a wornan who gave birth a few nights after the death of her husband. Abu Salama said
1247,Yahya related to me from Malik from Said ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujra from his paternal aunt
1248,Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki from Amr ibn Shuayb from Said ibn al-Musayyab that Umar ibn al-Khattab sent back widows from the desert and prevented them from doing the hajj
1249,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Saqd that he had heard that as-Sa'ib ibn Khabbab died
1250,Yahya related to me from Malik that Hisham ibn Urwa said about a Bedouin woman whose husband died
1251,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullan ibn Umar said, ""The only place a woman whose husband has died and a woman who is absolutely divorced can spend the night is in their houses"
1252,Yahya related to me from Malik that Yahya ibn Said said that he had heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad say that Zayd ibn Abd al-Malik separated some men and their wives who were slave-girls who had borne children to men who had died
1253,Malik related to me from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar said
1254,"Malik said, ""This is what is done among us."" Malik added, ""If she does not have a menstrual period, her idda is three months"
1255,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar said
1256,Yahya related to me the like of that from Malik from Ibn Shihab. Malik said
1257,Yahya related to me from Malik from Rabia ibn Abi Abd ar-Rahman from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban that Ibn Muhayriz said
1258,"And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, that he informed him: \Aisha"
1259,"And it was narrated to me from Malik, from Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, that he asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab about suckling. Sa'id said: \Anything that occurs within two years"
1260,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar did not practise coitus interruptus and thought that it was disapproved
1261,Yahya related to me from Malik from Damra ibn Said al-Mazini from al-Hajjaj ibn Amr ibn Ghaziya that he was sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit when Ibn Fahd came to him. He was from the Yemen. He said
1262,Yahya related to me from Malik from Humayd ibn Qays al-Makki that a man called Dhafif said that Ibn Abbas was asked about coitus interruptus. He called a slave-girl of his and said
1263,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm from Humayd ibn Nafi that Zaynab bint Abi Salama related these three traditions to him. Zaynab said
1264,"Zaynab said, ""I went to the house of Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when her brother had died. She called for perfume and put some on and said, 'By Allah! I have no need of perfume, but I heard the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say, 'It is not halal for a woman who trusts in Allah and the Last Day to abstain from adornment in mourning for someone who has died for more than three nights, except for four months and ten days for a husband"
1265,"Zaynab said, ""I heard my mother, Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said, 'Messenger of Allah! My daughter's husband died, and her eyes are troubling her, can she put kohl on them?' The Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, 'No' two or three times. Then he said, 'It is only four months and ten days. In the Jahiliyya, none of you threw away the piece of dung until a year had passed.' "" Humayd ibn Nafi said, ""I asked Zaynab to explain what 'throwing away the piece of dung at the end of a year' meant. Zaynab said, 'In the Jahiliyya when a woman's husband died, she went into a small tent and dressed in the worst of clothes. She did not touch perfume or anything until a year had passed. Then she was brought an animal - a donkey, a sheep, or a bird, and she would break her idda with it, by rubbing her body against it (taftaddu). Rarely did she break her idda with anything (by rubbing herself against it) but that it died. Then she would come out and would be given a piece of dung. She would throw it away and then return to whatever she wished of perfumes or whatever.' "" Malik explained, 'Taftaddu' means to wipe her skin with it in the same way as with a healing charm"
1266,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Safiyya bint Abi Ubayd from A'isha and Hafsa
1267,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umm Salama
1268,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Salim ibn Abdullah and Sulayman ibn Yasar said that if a woman whose husband had died feared that an inflammation of her eyes might affect her sight or that some complaint might befall her
1269,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafic that Saffiyya bint Abi Ubayd suffered from an eye-complaint while she was in mourning for her husband
1270,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the Messenger of Allah
1271,Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that Umm Salama
